I think that Nethack's elves are a playful amalgam of lots of different
types of elvendom, just as Nethack itself is such an amalgam.

Certainly, elves being chaotic has been questioned by enough people
over the years (myself one of them, a long time ago) that the DevTeam
must feel rather strongly about their decision.

The removal of the elven role, and its associated quest, from 3.4
removed a good number of Tolkien references from the vanilla game.


> In any case, I see no argument that Elves should be allowed to do
> "evil" things as a blanket rule.  Orcs, sure, they're portrayed as evil
> everywhere they appear, pretty much, but elves are portrayed as "not
> evil" or at least "only potentially evil" more often than not.

I predict a major turn-around in the fantasy-literature perception of
orcs in the near future, if it hasn't already begun.  Smart authors
will be wary of anything that can be termed "evil" without close
examination, because of the obvious correlation with racial turmoil in
our time.  Certainly, if I were writing fantasy at the moment, I'd see
there's serious hay to be made there.  It's had to have occured to
Terry Pratchett at some point, at least.

